# Keep the build context small and free of things that must never reach a
# public image layer or a build cache.
#
# Without this the whole repo - including .git, with every commit and any secret
# ever committed and later removed - is uploaded as build context. It does not
# land in the final image with the COPY lines this Dockerfile uses, but it is
# sent to the builder, it lands in the build cache, and a single careless
# `COPY . .` in future would publish all of it.
.git
.github
.gitignore
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
venv
tests
docs
examples
helm
infra
gateway_lambda
scripts
bin
*.md
!README.md
.env
*.pem
*.key
